# {{ repo_name }}

> {{ description }}

## What it is

A thin FastMCP server for **{{ service_display_name }}**, scaffolded for the
[`homelab-llm`][cockpit] cockpit. It starts with one placeholder endpoint-info
tool; replace that scaffold with service-specific read-only observations per
[ADR-0007][adr-0007].

## Install

The cockpit can run this repo directly from GitHub with `uvx`:

```bash
uvx --from git+https://github.com/{{ repo_owner }}/{{ repo_name }} {{ repo_name }}
```

Wire it into the cockpit by adding the `{{ service_name }}` MCP entry to
`homelab-llm`'s `.env.example` and `scripts/render-mcp-config.sh`.

## Environment

Required env vars (see `.env.example`):

| Var | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `{{ service_env_prefix }}_HOST` | {{ service_display_name }} host/IP, no scheme |
| `{{ service_env_prefix }}_USERNAME` | Dedicated MCP user |
| `{{ service_env_prefix }}_PASSWORD` | Password for that user |
| `{{ service_env_prefix }}_PORT` | Optional API port (default `{{ default_port }}`) |
| `{{ service_env_prefix }}_USE_HTTPS` | Optional, default `true` |

## Tools

- `{{ service_name | replace('-', '_') }}_get_endpoint_info()` — scaffold tool
  that proves settings, connection reuse, FastMCP registration, and tests work.
  Replace it with real {{ service_display_name }} tools before production use.

## Develop

This repo uses [`uv`][uv] for dependency / venv management.

```bash
uv sync
uv run ruff format .
uv run ruff check .
uv run mypy src
uv run pytest
uv run {{ repo_name }}
```

